  "data": {
    "body": "Starting from rest, a woman lifts a barbell of mass \\textit{m} with a constant force of F Newtons through a distance of \\textit{h} meters, at which point she is still lifting, and the barbell has acquired a speed of \\textit{v} m/s.\n\nLet $E_{\\textit{woman}}$ stand for the internal energy of the woman.\n\nFor the \\textbf{system} consisting of the \\textbf{woman + barbell}, which equation below is the correct application of the energy principle from the initial state with the barbell at rest to the final state with the barbell having moved upward a distance \\textit{h} and has a speed \\textit{v}?",
    "solution": [
      0
    ],
    "answerChoices": [
      {
        "id": "63cd5b47-1393-4ba4-81f3-b5673df13e6f",
        "index": 0,
        "body": "$\\triangle$$E_{\\textit{woman}}$ + $(\\frac{1}{2}mv^2 - 0)$ = - $mgh$",
        "questionId": "422374fd-15f0-4b24-886e-060cc6f0f2c5",
